{"id": "0712da4a-bf2b-4070-8824-c211a607e64b", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T01:38:03.730304", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "8f696be1-9669-45fb-a6fe-523b4308b30e", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "The repository is masked/empty. There is no zero-bubble pipeline parallelism code available. The task.json notes \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"\n\nSo my inspection finding: the repository contains only task.json; no pipeline parallelism implementation is present. I should report this honestly and propose a design approach based on the known reference implementation (the \"zero bubble pipeline parallelism\" paper by Qi et al. 2023, with the associated repo \"zero-bubble-pipeline-parallelism\" / \"PipeDream\"-style simulator, or Varflow). Actually the known repo: https://github.com/PKU-DAIR/Hetu - zero bubble in Hetu/DistMM? There's also \"1F1B-Interleaved\" in Megatron-LM (interleaved pipeline schedule, --num-layers-per-virtual-pipeline-stage), and ZB-H1 / ZB-H2 / ZB-V schedules in the \"Zero Bubble\" paper (Qi et al., arXiv:2305.10101) implemented in the Varflow / Hetu project. Also the paper by Andreessen et al. \"Efficiently Training Large Neural Networks with Zero Bubble Pipeline Parallelism\" (arXiv:2304.14604) defines ZB(1p) and ZB(2p) schedules — that's the Fan, Song, et al. \"Minimizing Pipeline Using Zero Bubble Pipeline Parallelism\" arXiv:2304.14604, which introduces ZB(1p) and ZB(2p) — matches the question's naming exactly (1F1B, 1F1B-I, ZB-1p, ZB-2p). That paper has a simulator? Their implementation is in JAX/TPU I think (\"We implement ZB schedules in JAX\"). Hmm.\n\nThere's also a known open-source repo: \"zero-bubble-schedules\" or the \"pipeline-schedules\" figure repo from Microsoft (ms-swift? deepspeed?). There's https://github.com/PKU-DAIR/Hetu-ZB (ZB-H1, ZB-H2). And there is a repo \"zero_bubble_pipeline_parallelism\" possibly with a simulator under `pipevdb`? Also FlexGEMM? Not sure.\n\nRegardless: I cannot verify. I