{"id": "087de92d-ae39-4551-9b3e-f35dfc2d2d9b", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T01:42:17.886086", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "812eb12c-d393-4f38-b09e-02a25de41630", "thought": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "He inspeccionado el entorno. Hallazgo clave y no obvio: **el repositorio está vacío/enmascarado**, así que la parte 1 de tu petición no puede responderse \"desde el source\". Te lo reporto tal cual, junto con la propuesta de enfoque."}], "reasoning_content": "Confirmed: no network (pip download fails), no numpy/torch, but Python 3.14 stdlib works, 224 CPUs.\n\nNow write the plan handoff. It should be in Spanish (researcher wrote in Spanish). Structure:\n\n1) Inspection findings — honest: repository is empty/masked (only task.json). No 1F1B/1F1B-I/ZB-1p/ZB-2p code, no simulators, no Megatron/DeepSpeed/Varflow, no GPU, no numpy/torch. So the \"named implementations\" question cannot be answered from source; I give the canonical naming map as an assumption to be confirmed by the researcher (Megatron-LM interleaved schedule `PipelineScheduleInterleaved1F1B` / `forward_backward_pipelining_with_interleaving`; zero-bubble repo `ZeroBubbleScheduler` with ZB-H1/ZB-H2/ZB-V; Fan et al. ZB(1p)/ZB(2p)). Also microbatches param names in those canonical repos (Megatron `--num-microbatches`, DeepSpeed `micro_batches`/`microbatch_extract`, Varflow `n_micro_batch`), and the analytic bubble formulas — but clearly mark as external knowledge / assumption, not repository observation.\n\nActually careful: don't overclaim about external repos. Present as \"canonical references to confirm with you\" and label as assumption.\n\n2) Approach proposal, one paragraph per point.\n\n3) Assumptions/uncertainties list.\n\nThen end_researcher_turn with stage=plan.\n\nLet me draft the metric:\n- Independent variable: m = número de microbatches por minibatch/iteración (entero), único factor manipulado.\n- Dependencia: throughput normalizado por dispositivo: T̂ = (m·B) / (p · t_iter) 